# Lab documentation contract (Yingson Labs)

**`lab-standards` is the source of truth for all Yingson Labs documentation.** Every other Yingson Labs repo is a **child**. Children extend it; they never contradict it.

Full contract: `lab-standards/LAB-DOC-CONTRACT.md` · Gitea: `gitea.yingson.com/jason/lab-standards`

> **Does NOT apply to WavePoint.** WavePoint has its own conventions, its own `DEC-###` sequence, GitHub-first paths, and `#service-alerts` (never `#alerts`). Never flow WavePoint decisions into `LAB-DECISIONS.md`.

---

## 🛑 The one rule that overrides convenience

**If two sources disagree, or ownership is unclear, or a slug/enum does not resolve — STOP and ALERT JASON. Do not guess. Do not silently pick a side.**

Guessing is faster and usually looks right. That is the problem. A verification pass in August 2026 found ten factual conflicts (`C-1`–`C-10` in `SERVICE-SLUG-REGISTRY.md`); **several would have been resolved wrongly by a confident guess** — including C-1, where every document said Plex and the answer was Jellyfin.

Continue any work that does not depend on the answer. Record both sides next to the data with a `⚠️ CONFLICT` block. Then ask:

```
⚠️ CONFLICT — needs your decision
**What disagrees:** A says <X>; B says <Y>
**Why it matters:** <what breaks if we pick wrong>
**How to settle it:** <specific command / UI page / question>
**What I did instead:** recorded both, changed nothing.
```

