## 🛑 Protected invariant — the NAS is on a different VLAN

The Ugreen NAS is at **`192.168.5.180` on the Home VLAN**; every service is on IoT (`192.168.30.0/24`), default-deny between them. **One UniFi allow rule carries all NFS traffic and the PBS datastore.**

**Never** delete, narrow, or reorder an inter-VLAN rule involving `192.168.5.180` or NFS without confirming what it carries. Breaking it produces **no firewall error** — just media, photos, and every backup failing at once, looking like unrelated service faults. `destructive` tier, human only.

